# wip252 ARP step 2a: a note (semitones) per Tonic track per step, project_t.note, patterns 1-16.
# The notes go with the trigs: a trig tapped off, FUNC + ACCENT / FILL (copy / paste), CLEAR TRACK and CLEAR PATTERN clear or copy them;
# they are saved and come back after a power cycle. (Nothing records them yet: notepoke is the host's stand-in for step 2b.)
wait 300
tap EDIT
expect view 14
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey w8
tapkey b2
tapkey w4
notepoke 0 0 0 7
notepoke 0 0 8 -5
notepoke 0 2 4 3
expect note0.0.0 7
expect note0.0.8 -5
expect note0.2.4 3
# copy pattern 1, paste into pattern 4: the notes come along, pattern 1 keeps its own
key b10 down
tapkey b8
key b10 up
key b10 down
tapkey w3
key b10 up
expect pattern 4
key b10 down
tapkey b9
key b10 up
expect note3.0.0 7
expect note3.0.8 -5
expect note3.2.4 3
expect note0.0.0 7
# a paste over a pattern replaces its notes too (pattern 4 got a stray note, then pattern 1 is pasted again)
notepoke 3 5 9 11
key b10 down
tapkey b9
key b10 up
expect note3.5.9 0
# back on pattern 1: a trig tapped off takes its note with it
key b10 down
tapkey w0
key b10 up
expect pattern 1
tapkey b0
tapkey w8
expect hit0.0.8 0
expect note0.0.8 0
expect note0.0.0 7
# autosave, power cycle: the notes are still there
wait 6000
reboot
expect note0.0.0 7
expect note3.0.0 7
expect note3.2.4 3
# CLEAR TRACK 1 of pattern 1 (FUNC + black key 1 + PLAY, OCT+): its notes go, track 3's stay
key b10 down
key b0 down
tap PLAY
key b0 up
key b10 up
tap OCT+
expect note0.0.0 0
expect note0.2.4 3
# CLEAR PATTERN (FUNC + PLAY, OCT+)
key b10 down
tap PLAY
key b10 up
tap OCT+
expect note0.2.4 0
expect note3.2.4 3
